<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21301] MDT can reissue client FID sequences after a failed seq_srv commit and restart</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21301</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Observedbehavior"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Observed behavior&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An MDT went read-only after encountering the ldiskfs fast-symlink bug described in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19121" title="ldiskfs/e2fsck mishandle fast symlink with external xattr inode" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19121"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19121&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. It remained online in read-only mode for many hours before being restarted. After the restart, we found overlapping FID sequence ranges held by different clients.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Suspectedmechanism"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Suspected mechanism&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The MDT allocates client FID sequences in batches and persists the reservation boundary in &lt;tt&gt;seq_srv&lt;/tt&gt;. &lt;tt&gt;range_alloc_set()&lt;/tt&gt; promotes the next batch before that boundary is durable. An error can leave the promoted batch active. In &lt;tt&gt;fid_store.c&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;seq_store_update()&lt;/tt&gt; does not propagate the &lt;tt&gt;dt_trans_stop()&lt;/tt&gt; return value, and &lt;tt&gt;seq_update_cb()&lt;/tt&gt; clears &lt;tt&gt;lss_need_sync&lt;/tt&gt; even when it receives a commit error.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the MDT continues serving sequence RPCs after ldiskfs goes read-only, it can still grant sequences from an active in-memory batch without starting a new journal transaction. If a client retains a sequence from an uncommitted batch across restart, the MDT can reload an older &lt;tt&gt;seq_srv&lt;/tt&gt; boundary and grant that same sequence to a different client.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The available logs do not establish when the overlapping sequences were first granted or which reservation failed to persist.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Expectedbehavior"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Expected behavior&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The MDT should grant sequences only after their reservation is durable. A failed reservation should leave the affected batch unavailable for allocation. Restart or failover should never cause the MDT to reissue a sequence already granted to a client.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Relatedissue"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Related issue&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17658" title="sanity check when ofd assign a new sequence to osp" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17658"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17658&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; covers a related OST-side sequence persistence issue.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>Lustre 2.15.5-based deployment with an ldiskfs MDT. The allocator paths below were also reviewed in upstream Lustre 2.15.5.</environment>
